  "Music tested the original timestamp list. Three clips in each of four reference-count strata (1 or fewer, 2–5, 6–12, over 12) were selected by SHA256(reel-blind-timing-v1/ + recording) from the 56 Modal holdouts and cut at 3.5 s, plus two controls. Everyday-first used ten mixtures and two background-only controls. Its responses informed a change to the compact presentation only.",
  "Everyday-confirmation used 14 different ESC-50 original recordings, ten further foreground mixtures and two unmodified backgrounds. The compact field lists confirmed times and their count by channel. With no confirmed peaks the field is omitted. Repeated runs of the same input can yield different counts.",
  "Absolute error is the sum of absolute count differences. Overcount and undercount refer to clip totals. The exploratory 95% interval resamples clips as pairs. Shared backgrounds and single model responses limit generalization."
